#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "How Ditana separates its installer engine from its configuration knowledge base to ship improvements instantly, audit decisions transparently, and accept contributions without touching code."
msgstr "Co che Ditana separa il motor da ses installatur da la basa da savida da sia configuraziun per furnir immediatamain meglieraziuns, per controllar las decisiuns en moda transparenta e per acceptar contribuziuns senza tutgar il code."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuration as data"
msgstr "Configuraziun sco datas"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"When an Arch update on a Tuesday morning requires a new workaround for a "
"specific Intel iGPU — what does a traditional installer do? Nothing, until "
"somebody patches the bash script that drives it, releases a new ISO (1–3 "
"GB), and waits for users to download it. Days at best, weeks more commonly."
msgstr ""
"Cura ch’in’actualisaziun dad Arch in mardi en damaun pretenda ina nova "
"schliaziun provisorica per ina tscherta iGPU dad Intel – tge fa in "
"installatur tradiziunal? Nagut, fin che insatgi adatta il script bash che al "
"maina, publitgescha in nov ISO (1 – 3 GB) e spetga che las utilisadras ed "
"ils utilisaders al telechargian. Dis en il meglier cas, pli savens emnas."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"Ditana takes a fundamentally different approach: **configuration as data.**"
msgstr ""
"Ditana tscherna ina via fundamentalmain differenta: **configuraziun sco "
"datas.**"

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three separate pieces"
msgstr "Trais parts separadas"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid "Ditana's architecture is split into three repositories:"
msgstr "L’architectura da Ditana è dividida en trais repositoris:"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**The Engine** ([`ditana-installer`](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-"
"installer)) — a small, generic program that knows *how* to draw dialogs, "
"partition disks, detect hardware, and run `pacstrap`."
msgstr ""
"**Il motor** ([`ditana-installer`](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-"
"installer)) – in pitschen program generic che sa *co* dissegnar dialogs, "
"crear partiziuns sin discs, identifitgar la hardware ed exequir `pacstrap`."

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**The Knowledge Base** ([`ditana-config`](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-"
"config)) — a structured database written in [KDL v2](https://kdl.dev). It "
"declares every setting, every hardware quirk, every package dependency, "
"every lifecycle script, and the logical relationships between them."
msgstr ""
"**La basa da savida** ([`ditana-config`](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-"
"config)) – ina banca da datas structurada, scritta en [KDL v2](https://"
"kdl.dev). Ella declera mintga parameter, mintga particularitad da la "
"hardware, mintga dependenza da pachets, mintga script dal ciclus da vita e "
"las relaziuns logicas tranter els."

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**The Package Pipeline** ([`ditana-build`](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-"
"build)) – what builds the packages the knowledge base names. Ditana's "
"repository stands upon Arch's, and the recipes in it are rebuilt from "
"source, reviewed and signed by that pipeline rather than taken as they come."
msgstr ""
"**La pipeline da pachets** ([`ditana-build`](https://github.com/acrion/"
"ditana-build)) – quai che construescha ils pachets che la basa da savida "
"numna. Il repositori da Ditana sa basa sin quel dad Arch, ed ils recepts en "
"el vegnan reconstruids dal code da funtauna, examinads e signads da questa "
"pipeline, empè da vegnir surpigliads tals sco ch’els èn."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"When you boot the Ditana ISO, the engine connects to GitHub and downloads "
"the latest release of the knowledge base (falling back to an offline "
"snapshot bundled with the ISO if you have no internet connection)."
msgstr ""
"Cura che Vus aviais l’ISO da Ditana, sa collia il motor cun GitHub e "
"telechargia l’ultima versiun da la basa da savida (sche Vus n’avais nagina "
"connexiun a l’internet, utilisescha el sco soluziun da reserva in snapshot "
"offline che vegn furnì cun l’ISO)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"What the runtime fetch does not cover is worth knowing too. The engine "
"itself and the converter it reads KDL with are on the medium and change only "
"with a new one. And the channel carries a mistake as readily as a fix: a "
"configuration that names a package the repository of an older medium cannot "
"serve makes that medium unable to install, which is exactly what happened "
"when Arch withdrew `bubblewrap-suid` in September 2026."
msgstr ""
"Er quai che la telechargiada durant l’execuziun na cuvra betg, vala la paina "
"da savair. Il motor sez ed il converter cun il qual el legia KDL sa chattan "
"sin il medium e sa midan mo cun in nov medium. Ed il chanal transporta in "
"sbagl tuttina facilmain sco ina correctura: ina configuraziun che numna in "
"pachet ch’il repositori d’in medium pli vegl na po betg furnir, renda quel "
"medium incapabel d’installar – quai è capità exactamain cura ch’Arch ha "
"retratg `bubblewrap-suid` il settember 2026."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why this matters"
msgstr "Pertge che quai è impurtant"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid "Three benefits, in order of immediate impact:"
msgstr "Trais avantatgs, en l’urden da lur effect immediat:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Zero-respin updates.** If a user reports that a recent Arch update "
"requires a new workaround, the fix lands in `ditana-config` as a small KDL "
"edit. The very next person who boots a Ditana ISO downloads the updated "
"logic automatically. The fix reaches users immediately, without anyone "
"needing to download a new ISO."
msgstr ""
"**Actualisaziuns senza crear in nov ISO.** Sch’ina utilisadra u in "
"utilisader annunzia ch’in’actualisaziun recenta dad Arch pretenda ina nova "
"schliaziun provisorica, arriva la correctura en `ditana-config` sco pitschna "
"modificaziun da KDL. Gia la proxima persuna che aviescha in ISO da Ditana "
"telechargia automaticamain la logica actualisada. La correctura cuntanscha "
"las utilisadras ed ils utilisaders immediatamain, senza che insatgi stoppia "
"telechargiar in nov ISO."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Transparent reasoning.** Because settings are declared as structured data "
"with explicit conditions, the rules are auditable end-to-end. Anyone can "
"read the KDL files and see exactly *why* a package is installed, *what* "
"combination of settings triggers a configuration file to be deployed, or "
"*which* hardware property gates an option. No bash detective work."
msgstr ""
"**Raschunament transparent.** Cunquai ch’ils parameters èn declerads sco "
"datas structuradas cun cundiziuns explicitas, pon las reglas vegnir "
"controlladas dal cumenzament fin a la fin. Mintga persuna po leger las "
"datotecas KDL e vesair exactamain *pertge* ch’in pachet vegn installà, *tge* "
"cumbinaziun da parameters fa ch’ina datoteca da configuraziun vegn "
"installada u *tge* caracteristica da la hardware furma la barriera per "
"in’opziun. Nagina lavur da detectiv en bash."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Forkable contributions.** Adding a hardware workaround, a new desktop "
"tweak, or a new packaging choice typically involves modifying a single KDL "
"file. No installer engine modifications – and outside hardware detectors, "
"which are one-line Raku expressions, no Raku at all. The `ditana-config` "
"README walks contributors through the schema; most pull requests touch one "
"file."
msgstr ""
"**Contribuziuns via fork.** Agiuntar ina schliaziun provisorica per la "
"hardware, ina nova adattaziun dal desktop u ina nova tscherna da pachets "
"pretenda per regla da modifitgar ina suletta datoteca KDL. Naginas "
"modificaziuns vi dal motor da l’installatur – e cun excepziun dals detecturs "
"da la hardware, ch’èn expressiuns da Raku d’ina lingia, insumma nagin Raku. "
"Il README da `ditana-config` maina las persunas che contribueschan tras il "
"schema; la gronda part dals pull requests tutga ina suletta datoteca."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why KDL, not JSON or YAML"
msgstr "Pertge KDL e betg JSON u YAML"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"The knowledge base could have been any structured format. KDL was chosen "
"because it has the properties Ditana's configuration actually needs:"
msgstr ""
"La basa da savida avess pudì avair mintga format structurà. KDL è vegnì "
"tschernì, perquai ch’el ha las caracteristicas che la configuraziun da "
"Ditana dovra propi:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Native comments.** YAML and JSON both struggle here — YAML has comments "
"but tooling support is uneven; JSON has none at all. Ditana's settings "
"include extensive rationale comments explaining *why* a default is what it "
"is. Those comments are the point."
msgstr ""
"**Commentaris nativs.** YAML e JSON han omadus difficultads qua – YAML ha "
"commentaris, ma il sustegn tras ils utensils è irregular; JSON n’ha insumma "
"nagins. Ils parameters da Ditana cuntegnan commentaris detagliads che "
"explitgeschan *pertge* ch’ina valur da standard è sco ch’ella è. Quests "
"commentaris èn l’essenzial."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Raw strings.** Embedded shell snippets, sed expressions, and regex "
"patterns are first-class. No double-escaping `\"` and `\\` to satisfy the "
"parser."
msgstr ""
"**Strings crivs.** Fragments da shell integrads, expressiuns da sed e "
"patruns da regex èn elements da plaina valur. `\"` e `\\` na ston betg "
"vegnir mascrads duas giadas per ch’il parser als acceptia."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Hierarchical without ceremony.** Children, properties, and arguments "
"coexist cleanly. The same node can describe a setting *and* contain sub-"
"nodes for its packages, scripts, and files."
msgstr ""
"**Ierarchic senza ceremonias.** Nufs subordinads, proprietads ed arguments "
"existan en moda clera in sper l’auter. Il medem nuf po descriver in "
"parameter *e* cuntegnair nufs subordinads per ses pachets, scripts e "
"datotecas."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Diff-friendly.** Insertion order is preserved. A code review of a one-line "
"addition shows a one-line diff, not a reordered structure."
msgstr ""
"**Adattà per diffs.** L’urden d’inserziun resta mantegnì. Ina revisiun dal "
"code d’ina lingia agiuntada mussa in diff d’ina lingia, betg ina structura "
"reordinada."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"The format is parsed by a small Rust converter (`json-kdl-converter`, also "
"versioned alongside the schema) before the Raku installer consumes it as "
"JSON. The next section explains how the data is validated end-to-end before "
"any of that."
msgstr ""
"Il format vegn analisà d’in pitschen converter en Rust (`json-kdl-"
"converter`, che vegn er gestì en versiuns ensemen cun il schema), avant che "
"l’installatur en Raku l’elavura sco JSON. La proxima secziun explitgescha co "
"che las datas vegnan validadas dal cumenzament fin a la fin avant tut quai."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "What this looks like in practice"
msgstr "Co che quai vesa or en la pratica"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid "A complete, working setting in `ditana-config` looks like this:"
msgstr "In parameter cumplet che funcziuna en `ditana-config` vesa or uschia:"

#. type: Fenced code block (kdl)
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"// XFCE fallback for Wayland-only primary terminals (foot, cosmic-term).\n"
"// Fires when the user picks a Wayland-native terminal AND also installs\n"
"// XFCE. Writes to xfce-xdg-terminals.list only; xdg-terminals.list still\n"
"// points at the primary terminal for Wayland sessions.\n"
"- name=\"fallback-kitty-for-xfce\" \\\n"
"  default-value=\"`(install-foot OR install-cosmic-term) AND install-xfce`\" {\n"
"    arch-packages \"kitty\" \\\n"
"                  \"imagemagick\" \\\n"
"                  \"python-pygments\" \\\n"
"                  \"libcanberra\" \\\n"
"                  \"xdg-terminal-exec-git\"\n"
"    files \"/etc/xdg/kitty/kitty.conf\" \\\n"
"          \"/usr/share/pixmaps/ditana-logo-tiny.png\"\n"
"    chroot-script \"mkdir -p /etc/xdg\" \\\n"
"                  \"echo kitty.desktop >/etc/xdg/xfce-xdg-terminals.list\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"// XFCE fallback for Wayland-only primary terminals (foot, cosmic-term).\n"
"// Fires when the user picks a Wayland-native terminal AND also installs\n"
"// XFCE. Writes to xfce-xdg-terminals.list only; xdg-terminals.list still\n"
"// points at the primary terminal for Wayland sessions.\n"
"- name=\"fallback-kitty-for-xfce\" \\\n"
"  default-value=\"`(install-foot OR install-cosmic-term) AND install-xfce`\" {\n"
"    arch-packages \"kitty\" \\\n"
"                  \"imagemagick\" \\\n"
"                  \"python-pygments\" \\\n"
"                  \"libcanberra\" \\\n"
"                  \"xdg-terminal-exec-git\"\n"
"    files \"/etc/xdg/kitty/kitty.conf\" \\\n"
"          \"/usr/share/pixmaps/ditana-logo-tiny.png\"\n"
"    chroot-script \"mkdir -p /etc/xdg\" \\\n"
"                  \"echo kitty.desktop >/etc/xdg/xfce-xdg-terminals.list\"\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"That node declares a derived setting with no dialog of its own, a logical "
"expression over three other settings, the packages to install when it holds, "
"and the file that makes XFCE use them. The reasoning stands next to the "
"rule, where someone reviewing it can see why. The full schema documentation "
"is in the [`ditana-config` README](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-"
"config#readme)."
msgstr ""
"Quest nuf declera in parameter derivà senza agen dialog, in’expressiun "
"logica sur trais auters parameters, ils pachets che vegnan installads cura "
"ch’ella è vaira, e la datoteca che fa ch’XFCE als utilisescha. La motivaziun "
"stat sper la regla, nua ch’ina persuna che l’examinescha po vesair pertge. "
"La documentaziun cumpletta dal schema sa chatta en il [README da `ditana-"
"config`](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-config#readme)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"The same shape carries things that are not packages at all. A program that "
"needs an unprivileged user namespace for its sandbox says so beside itself:"
msgstr ""
"La medema furma porta er chaussas che n’èn insumma nagins pachets. In "
"program che dovra in spazi da num da l’utilisader senza privilegis per ses "
"sandbox, di quai directamain sper sasez:"

#. type: Fenced code block (kdl)
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- name=\"flatpak\" default-value=#true {\n"
"    arch-packages \"flatpak\"\n"
"    // Every Flatpak, not only the browsers, runs bwrap to build its outer\n"
"    // sandbox, and bwrap needs a user namespace. This is the declaration\n"
"    // that buys it one.\n"
"    userns-allow \"/usr/bin/bwrap\"\n"
"  }\n"
msgstr ""
"- name=\"flatpak\" default-value=#true {\n"
"    arch-packages \"flatpak\"\n"
"    // Every Flatpak, not only the browsers, runs bwrap to build its outer\n"
"    // sandbox, and bwrap needs a user namespace. This is the declaration\n"
"    // that buys it one.\n"
"    userns-allow \"/usr/bin/bwrap\"\n"
"  }\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"Ditana does not hand unprivileged user namespaces to each program. A minimal "
"BPF program, [`ditana-userns-guard`](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-userns-"
"guard), is attached to the kernel's own `userns_create` hook and refuses a "
"namespace to any executable that a setting has not requested. A hook of that "
"kind can only refuse and never grant, which is why the sysctl that switches "
"namespaces off is raised only once the program is loaded – a machine that "
"cannot load it keeps them off entirely. This is the default state of a "
"System Hardening option; switch it off and namespaces are open to "
"everything, as they are on most distributions."
msgstr ""
"Ditana na dat betg spazis da num da l’utilisader senza privilegis a mintga "
"program. In program BPF minimal, [`ditana-userns-guard`](https://github.com/"
"acrion/ditana-userns-guard), è collià cun il hook `userns_create` dal kernel "
"sez e refusa in spazi da num a mintga program exequibel ch’in parameter n’ha "
"betg dumandà. In hook da quest tip po mo refusar e mai conceder, perquai "
"vegn il sysctl che deactivescha ils spazis da num augmentà pir cura ch’il "
"program è chargià – ina maschina che na po betg chargiar il program lascha "
"ils spazis da num dal tuttafatg deactivads. Quai è il stadi da standard "
"d’in’opziun da System Hardening; deactivai quella, ed ils spazis da num èn "
"averts per tut, sco sin la gronda part da las distribuziuns."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"Ditana refuses user namespaces to everything that has not asked. What makes "
"that workable is that the request is local: it is written where the package "
"is chosen, so nothing needs to keep a synchronized central list, and "
"switching the setting off takes the permission with it. The installer "
"collects the declarations of the settings that ultimately remain enabled and "
"generates the allowlist from those."
msgstr ""
"Ditana refusa spazis da num da l’utilisader a tut quai che n’ha betg "
"dumandà. Quai che fa funcziunar quest sistem è che la dumonda è locala: ella "
"vegn scritta là nua ch’il pachet vegn tschernì, uschia ch’i na dovra nagina "
"glista centrala sincronisada, e la deactivaziun dal parameter allontanescha "
"er la permissiun. L’installatur rimna las decleraziuns dals parameters che "
"restan activads a la fin e generescha or da quellas la glista da permissiuns."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Validation: catching mistakes before they ship"
msgstr "Validaziun: chattar sbagls avant ch’els vegnan furnids"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"A knowledge base this large needs guardrails. Every commit — both locally "
"via [pre-commit hooks](https://pre-commit.com) and remotely on GitHub "
"Actions — runs a layered validation pipeline that catches the mistakes a "
"human reviewer might miss:"
msgstr ""
"Ina basa da savida uschè gronda dovra mesiras da protecziun. Mintga commit – "
"tant localmain tras [hooks pre-commit](https://pre-commit.com) sco er a "
"distanza sin GitHub Actions – exequescha ina pipeline da validaziun cun "
"plirs nivels che chatta ils sbagls ch’ina persuna che examinescha il code "
"pudess survesair:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid "**KDL syntax** (`kdlfmt`) — the file parses at all."
msgstr "**Sintaxa KDL** (`kdlfmt`) – la datoteca po insumma vegnir analisada."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Schema validation** ([`ditana-schema.json`](https://github.com/acrion/"
"ditana-config/blob/main/ditana-schema.json)) — every field has the right "
"type, no unknown properties, no missing required fields. Catches typos in "
"field names like `arc-packages` instead of `arch-packages`."
msgstr ""
"**Validaziun dal schema** ([`ditana-schema.json`](https://github.com/acrion/"
"ditana-config/blob/main/ditana-schema.json)) – mintga champ ha il tip "
"correct, naginas proprietads nunenconuschentas, nagins champs obligatorics "
"che mancan. Chatta sbagls da tippar en nums da champs sco `arc-packages` "
"empè da `arch-packages`."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**File reference integrity** — every file referenced from a setting actually "
"exists in `folders/`; conversely, every file in `folders/` is referenced by "
"at least one setting. Orphans get flagged. Directory references (which would "
"silently do nothing because the installer uses `cp` without `-R`) are "
"rejected."
msgstr ""
"**Integritad da las referenzas a datotecas** – mintga datoteca a la quala in "
"parameter fa referenza exista propi en `folders/`; a l’inversa fa almain in "
"parameter referenza a mintga datoteca en `folders/`. Datotecas orfnas vegnan "
"annunziadas. Referenzas ad ordinaturs (che na faschessan nagut, e quai senza "
"avis, perquai che l’installatur utilisescha `cp` senza `-R`) vegnan "
"refusadas."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Lifecycle correctness** — `chroot-script` lines that touch `/etc/skel/` "
"are rejected, because the user is created *after* `chroot-script` runs — the "
"correct field is `early-chroot-script`. A subtle bug that would otherwise "
"produce a system where the new user's home doesn't have the expected files."
msgstr ""
"**Correctadad dal ciclus da vita** – lingias da `chroot-script` che tutgan `/"
"etc/skel/` vegnan refusadas, perquai che l’account d’utilisader vegn creà "
"*suenter* l’execuziun da `chroot-script` – il champ correct è `early-chroot-"
"script`. In sbagl subtil che produciss uschiglio in sistem, en il qual "
"l’ordinatur persunal dal nov account d’utilisader na cuntegna betg las "
"datotecas spetgadas."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Shell script validity** – every shell snippet in any of the script-list "
"fields gets `bash -n` for syntax and [`shellcheck`](https://"
"www.shellcheck.net) for quality. A missing quote or a `[ \"$x\" = $y ]` "
"style bug is detected at commit time, not at first install."
msgstr ""
"**Validitad dals scripts da shell** – mintga fragment da shell en in dals "
"champs cun glistas da scripts vegn controllà cun `bash -n` per la sintaxa e "
"cun [`shellcheck`](https://www.shellcheck.net) per la qualitad. In segn da "
"citaziun che manca u in sbagl dal tip `[ \"$x\" = $y ]` vegn identifitgà al "
"mument dal commit, betg pir tar l’emprima installaziun."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Declared permissions and kernel settings** – a `userns-allow` entry must "
"be an absolute path, and a `sysctl` entry must name something that is a "
"sysctl key and give it a value the kernel will take. Both fields were added "
"in 0.9.4 and are declared in [`ditana-schema.json`](https://github.com/"
"acrion/ditana-config/blob/main/ditana-schema.json)."
msgstr ""
"**Permissiuns e parameters dal kernel declerads** – in’endataziun `userns-"
"allow` sto esser in percurs absolut, ed in’endataziun `sysctl` sto numnar "
"insatge ch’è ina clav sysctl e dar ad ella ina valur ch’il kernel accepta. "
"Omadus champs èn vegnids agiuntads en la versiun 0.9.4 e vegnan declerads en "
"[`ditana-schema.json`](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-config/blob/main/"
"ditana-schema.json)."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Contradicting kernel settings** – two settings that write the same sysctl "
"key with different values stop the installation, and the message names both "
"of them. Assembled as shell text, as it was before 0.9.4, the last line "
"written simply won and nobody was told."
msgstr ""
"**Parameters dal kernel cuntradictorics** – dus parameters che scrivan la "
"medema clav sysctl cun valurs differentas ferman l’installaziun, ed il "
"messadi numna omadus. Cura ch’ils parameters vegnivan cumponids sco text da "
"shell, sco avant la versiun 0.9.4, gudagnava simplamain l’ultima lingia "
"scritta, e nagin na vegniva infurmà."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"**Logical expression integrity** — backticks must balance; every setting "
"name referenced in a `default-value` or `available` expression must actually "
"exist somewhere in the knowledge base. A typo like `install-cosmik` instead "
"of `install-cosmic` gets caught at commit time instead of producing a silent "
"runtime crash."
msgstr ""
"**Integritad da las expressiuns logicas** – ils accents grevs ston furmar "
"pèrs; mintga num da parameter al qual in’expressiun `default-value` u "
"`available` fa referenza sto propi exister insanua en la basa da savida. In "
"sbagl da tippar sco `install-cosmik` empè da `install-cosmic` vegn chattà al "
"mument dal commit, empè da chaschunar in collaps silenzius durant "
"l’execuziun."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/configuration-as-data.md
msgid ""
"The full check runs in seconds locally with `pre-commit run --all-files`, "
"and again on every push to GitHub. Local green means CI green; broken "
"commits never make it to a release."
msgstr ""
"Il test cumplet dura localmain paucas secundas cun `pre-commit run --all-"
"files` e vegn exequì anc ina giada tar mintga push sin GitHub. Verd "
"localmain munta verd en il CI; commits defects na cuntanschan mai ina "
"versiun."

